#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091980 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ed5facf-f654-5890-974f-bbdcd9641515" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem to Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "7e804bd6-9ddf-58cb-8013-0c0623ecdd07" :question/math-academy-id "e-5270" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{1}{\\left[ \\cos (\\theta) +\\textrm{i}\\sin(\\theta) \\right]^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\left[ \\cos(\\theta) +\\textrm{i}\\sin(\\theta) \\right]^2} = \\left[ \\cos(\\theta) +\\textrm{i}\\sin(\\theta) \\right]^{-2} .\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\left[ \\cos(\\varphi) + \\textrm{i}\\sin(\\varphi) \\right]^n = \\cos(n\\varphi) + \\textrm{i}\\sin{(n\\varphi)}.\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-2$ and $\\varphi=\\theta.$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{2}} & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\cos(-\\varphi) = \\cos (\\varphi)$ and $\\sin(-\\varphi) = -\\sin(\\varphi)$ for any input $\\varphi,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos(-2\\theta) + \\textrm{i}\\sin(-2\\theta) = \\cos(2\\theta) - \\textrm{i}\\sin{(2\\theta)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091981 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5055bd50-a6aa-547d-9ce3-573d79ac2e91" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "cbd9cb3f-bb2e-5505-8f53-068e77717edb" :question/math-academy-id "e-5271" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\left[ \\cos \\left( \\dfrac{\\theta}{10} \\right) + \\textrm{i}\\sin \\left( \\dfrac{\\theta}{10}\\right) \\right]^4.$" :question/worked-solution "De Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\left[ \\cos(\\varphi) + \\textrm{i}\\sin(\\varphi) \\right]^n = \\cos(n\\varphi) + \\textrm{i}\\sin{(n\\varphi)}.\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=4$ and $\\varphi=\\dfrac{\\theta}{10}.$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{10})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{10})]}^{4} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\theta }{10})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\theta }{10}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\theta }{5})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\theta }{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091987 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc91582-8d44-5de1-9c98-1c5de173eefb" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem With a Negative Sine"}] :question/id #uuid "ea0c744c-8814-5a78-8059-23346051ef1a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5291" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{1}{\\left[ \\cos (2\\theta) -\\textrm{i}\\sin (2\\theta) \\right]^4}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )]}^{4}} & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )]}^{-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\left[ \\cos (\\varphi) - \\textrm{i}\\sin(\\varphi) \\right]^n = \\cos(n\\varphi) - \\textrm{i}\\sin{(n\\varphi)}.\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-4$ and $\\varphi=2\\theta.$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )]}^{-4} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-4\\cdot 2\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4\\cdot 2\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-8\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\cos(-\\varphi) = \\cos (\\varphi)$ and $\\sin(-\\varphi) = -\\sin(\\varphi)$ for any input $\\varphi,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-8\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-[-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333280 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5055bd50-a6aa-547d-9ce3-573d79ac2e91" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "659e8513-2b5e-5949-a114-5ecd71568e77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(20\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333282} {:answer/id #uuid "5a775389-70eb-56c4-b38c-57f6cd9f9e71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333283} {:answer/id #uuid "6de6864a-2fb7-5d79-96ce-898e9c30f2b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\theta }{5})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\theta }{5})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333284} {:answer/id #uuid "d4773505-a917-5a62-a039-1d290a9fdc6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333285} {:answer/id #uuid "2f1a36ef-2260-5832-bf2b-c882a4d5664e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(20\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\theta ))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a775389-70eb-56c4-b38c-57f6cd9f9e71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333283} :answer-field/id #uuid "633f136e-0b06-5164-93a3-82f31b638a10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field