2186333291} {:answer/id #uuid "54c1715b-f971-5096-9491-1c70648c27bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333292} {:answer/id #uuid "331656ee-004b-503d-9bfd-9dd20325991f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54c1715b-f971-5096-9491-1c70648c27bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333292} :answer-field/id #uuid "062dbebe-305a-56c5-8611-abf6286429e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8fdc10d8-c29b-5c00-b56a-60501ddc763f" :question/math-academy-id "q-104122" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{2}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]^{4}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]^{4}}=2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]^{-4}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\phi ]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-4$ and $\\phi =2\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]^{4}} & =2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]^{-4} \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(-4)\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(-4)\\theta )] \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-8\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-8\\theta )]=2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333294 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ed5facf-f654-5890-974f-bbdcd9641515" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem to Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb36adf6-4486-57b2-914d-d3ba9356fbdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta )]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333296} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b62da0-c9d0-5068-ae1f-6c3f5404d834" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333297} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f1d326-dc24-506a-8d86-6dc7cc6c2859" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\theta }{5})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\theta }{5})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333298} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a664c0-1a25-504c-875d-cd9218a0d0f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333299} {:answer/id #uuid "e30ac6e0-6e0d-5d5a-aa21-963d4c43fbcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{5})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{5})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb36adf6-4486-57b2-914d-d3ba9356fbdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta )]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333296} :answer-field/id #uuid "5100cd51-625c-5fb8-93f6-d16afa91a0a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333295}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b275ef4-ffb1-58e0-a866-04afebd02244" :question/math-academy-id "q-104343" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{6}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{5}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{5}}=[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{-5}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\phi ]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-5$ and $\\phi =3\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{5}} & =6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ]^{-5} \\\\  & =6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(-5)\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3(-5)\\theta )] \\\\  & =6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-15\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-15\\theta )]=6[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta )].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333301 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ed5facf-f654-5890-974f-bbdcd964151