rname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-5\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta )-[-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333333 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc91582-8d44-5de1-9c98-1c5de173eefb" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem With a Negative Sine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a10e7dc-59ad-5956-951c-340a9d09343b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(6\\theta)+i\\sin(6\\theta)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a10e7dc-59ad-5956-951c-340a9d09343b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(6\\theta)+i\\sin(6\\theta)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333335} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5c69ea6-ddc7-59c6-be64-035b57c602f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0da530cd-bf3f-5ec6-96d1-51d45b4e7c87" :question/math-academy-id "q-325344" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]^{6}}$ in the form $x+\\text{i}y,$ where $x$ and $y$ are functions of $\\theta .$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]^{6}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{6}} & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-6$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-6}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-6\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-6\\theta )\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-6\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-6\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta )-[-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta )] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ed5facf-f654-5890-974f-bbdcd9641515" :knowledge-point/title "Applying De Moivre's Theorem to Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ed5c850-554e-5e02-8b2d-fee00e394146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta )+2\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333338} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ad7459-c625-567e-8ff0-43fcff9345fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-3\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333339} {:answer/id #uuid "a4feb6b3-c3db-50e4-bad6-121212965415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+6\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333340} {:answer/id #uuid "24f50184-7a71-5e1e-ac76-6b7c7e9237a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta )+\\text{i}\